From: realazizk <azizk@tuta.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:42:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] screenshare: don't copy a pending cursor frame through a
 disabled monitor

Backport of hyprwm/Hyprland#16533 (8010b4e). A pending cursor capture frame
kept the monitor it was captured on; after the monitor was removed, the next
cursor change (or a capture on the gone output) rendered into the capture
buffer through it: SIGSEGV in beginFullFakeRender() from
CCursorshareSession::copy(). copy() now refuses a disabled monitor.
---
 src/managers/screenshare/CursorshareSession.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/managers/screenshare/CursorshareSession.cpp b/src/managers/screenshare/CursorshareSession.cpp
index 1bd57ca..87b4cd8 100644
--- a/src/managers/screenshare/CursorshareSession.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/screenshare/CursorshareSession.cpp
@@ -200,7 +200,7 @@ static bool copyThemeCursorToShm(SP<IHLBuffer> buffer, wl_client* client, const
 }
 
 bool CCursorshareSession::copy() {
-    if (!m_pendingFrame.callback || !m_pendingFrame.monitor || !m_pendingFrame.callback || !m_pendingFrame.sourceBoxCallback)
+    if (!m_pendingFrame.callback || !m_pendingFrame.monitor || !m_pendingFrame.monitor->m_enabled || !m_pendingFrame.callback || !m_pendingFrame.sourceBoxCallback)
         return false;
 
     // FIXME: this doesn't really make sense but just to be safe
